//
// Normative rule hideleg_op (src/priv/hypervisor.adoc):
//   An interrupt that has been delegated to HS-mode (using mideleg) is further delegated to VS-mode
//     if the corresponding hideleg bit is set.
//
// Context:
//   mideleg bits 2, 6, 10 are read-only one, so every VS-level interrupt reaches HS-mode
//     delegation. A delegated interrupt is enabled by vsie (alias of hie) and, in VS-mode, by
//     vsstatus.SIE; in VU-mode it is always globally enabled. Interrupts for a more privileged mode
//     are taken first (machine.adoc: interrupts for higher-privilege modes are serviced before
//     those for lower-privilege modes).
//
// Test plan:
//   For VSSI, VSTI and VSEI with hideleg bit 1 and hie bit 1:
//   1. VS-mode, vsstatus.SIE = 1: taken by the VS-mode handler (xPP/xPV record VS).
//   2. VS-mode, vsstatus.SIE = 0: not taken.
//   3. VU-mode, vsstatus.SIE = 0: taken by the VS-mode handler (from VU).
//   4. Mixed destinations in VS-mode with vsstatus.SIE = 1: VSSI delegated and VSTI not, both
//     pending: VSTI is taken in HS-mode first, then VSSI in VS-mode.
//
// Approximate dynamic instruction count: 3247
//

